<title>USA: NYMEX to lower natgas futures spread margins Mon.</title>
<headline>NYMEX to lower natgas futures spread margins Mon.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-01-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>The New York Mercantile Exchange (NYMEX) said Monday it will decrease margins on spreads involving second month Henry Hub natural gas futures as of the close of business today.</p>
<p>The rates will be lowered to $500 from $3,800 for clearing members; to $550 from $4,180 for customers; and to $675 from $5,130 for customers, NYMEX said in a statement.</p>
<p>((--New York Power Desk 212-859-1624))</p>
</text>
